/// MonitorSupervisor — DynamicSupervisor managing every `Monitor` actor.
///
/// `CheckRegistry` starts children through this supervisor instead of
/// calling `Monitor spawnWith:` directly, so a crash in one check's
/// `Monitor` (e.g. an unhandled error inside its `HealthCheck check`) gets
/// an automatic OTP restart — per `Monitor supervisionPolicy` (`#permanent`)
/// — instead of silently going dark until someone notices and re-adds the
/// check by hand.
///
/// See SPEC.md §3, §10.
DynamicSupervisor(Monitor) subclass: MonitorSupervisor

  class childClass => Monitor
